# The kernel built without features (no `debug`, no `selftest`) boots and
# says nothing (docs/design.md, "A release kernel without UART code"): the
# loader prints as always, then COM1 stays silent. With no `test=` the
# kernel starts the root task, whose first DebugPutChar is an UnknownSyscall
# fault there; root has no fault handler, so it stops, silently, and the
# kernel idles. Nothing can end the run before the `uart` server and an
# IOPort capability for isa-debug-exit, so the scenario passes if the guest
# is still running, quiet, at the timeout: a release-kernel panic would have
# exited with failure, and a triple fault would have ended QEMU. The
# `release` scenario checks the same kernel through uart and console.
kernel: release
exit: timeout
timeout: 15
expect: microL4 loader
expect: memory regions; entering kernel
# What a kernel with `debug` prints.
forbid: microL4 kernel
forbid: bootinfo:
forbid: DEBUG HALT
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
